AD  - Space Technology Centre, AGH University of Science and Technology, Mickiewicza Ave. 30, Krakow, 30-059, Poland
AD  - Analog Astronaut Training Center, Kolo Strzelnicy 8A, Krakow, 30-219, Poland
AB  - Time perception is one of the factors that affect work efficiency and performance at work, especially during isolation, especially in space. In this study we present an idea of improvement of time perception measurement using Android OS based app for time perception measurement and work efficiency evaluation. The app was implemented using MVVM architecture and offered two tasks - passive and active time perception. In both tasks simple shape appeared and disappeared on the screen after given amount of time. In the first task, user had to guess and type how much time passed when the shape has been visible, in the second he was asked to hold the button for the same amount of time. Each analog astronaut had to perform a time perception test each day during their mission. All the results have been sent and analysed on the server. Authors propose also methods for work efficiency measurement - using the questionnaire or specially designed app. Work efficiency and subjective time perception also depended on analog astronauts physical activity which we observed based on the results. Finally, the role of Mission Control Center crew has been discussed, as well as its impact on work efficiency and time perception. Copyright © 2022 by the International Astronautical Federation (IAF). All rights reserved.
