AB  - This study explores how a Lean method collaborates with the UX characteristics to implement a single sign on application for the 'Y Generation' age group to monitor their daily academic life. With a personalized mobile application, students will be able to monitor their academic and/or nonacademic activities that scheduled every day. Lean UX will support the development phase by creating a minimum viable product (MVP) fast as possible during several steps or iterations. The UI / UX experiment results generated through two iterations with Think Aloud Interview Testing and Software Usability Testing. The results obtained are used to represent the user acceptance during User Experience testing with increasing SUS score to 72.85 and decreasing average time completion, which indicates an increasing point of cognitive process of the users as 80% while interacting with the application. © 2019 IEEE.
