AB  - The Internet of Things (IoT) is one of the most notable digital developments in recent years. As the Smart Revolution advances beyond its conceptual stage, the furniture sector emerges inside the IoT market. This paper proposes the transformation of ordinary furniture into an IoT system realized using the ESP32 microcontroller. Furthermore, the furniture is enriched with the ability to be controllable via the Android application over Bluetooth technology. Given the rise of devices and things enriched by IoT technologies, the application to manage these devices should be of such an architecture that it can be easily modified. This paper emphasizes the importance of application development following clean architecture principles that makes the application robust, easily upgradeable with new features, maintainable, and effortlessly testable. Such an approach would significantly reduce future efforts to control IoT devices using a mobile application. © 2022 IEEE.
