TI  - A Smart Mobile Waste Sorting App Based on Clean Architecture with Product Classification using Random Forest and KNN
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 International Conference on ICT for Smart Society, ICISS 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ICISS66954.2025.11389502
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105035346203?origin=resultslist
AD  - School of Electrical Engineering, Telkom University, Bandung, Indonesia
AD  - Telkom University, Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Bandung, Indonesia
AB  - This work presents the development of a mobile application for automatic waste classification using barcode decoding and machine learning techniques. The system is designed with a clean architecture approach to enhance maintainability, scalability, and modularity. A dataset of over 10,000 product entries was compiled and preprocessed to train two machine learning models: Random Forest and K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN). Both models classify waste types (organic or inorganic) based on barcode metadata and product names, with the Random Forest model achieving a superior validation accuracy of 97.7% and an average F1-score of 0.98, indicating robust and consistent classification performance. The application also integrates a reward system and is evaluated using the Technology Acceptance Model (TAM). Results show high user acceptance, with perceived usefulness (86.03 %), perceived ease of use (85.04 %), and behavioral intention to use (86.01 %). This work demonstrates a promising approach to digital waste management by combining product recognition, intelligent classification, and user-centered evaluation. © 2025 IEEE.
